---
const skills = [
  "HTML5", "CSS3", "JavaScript", "React.js", 
  "Next.js", "Astro.js", "Node.js", "Electron.js", 
  "Tailwind CSS", "Git"
];
---

<section id="about-section" class="portfolio-section">
    <div class="section-container">
        <div class="section-header">
            <span class="section-tag">02 / BIOGRAPHY &amp; SKILLS</span>
            <h2 class="section-title about-title">My Approach</h2>
        </div>

        <div class="about-body-content">
            <p class="about-para">
                As a JavaScript developer, I believe the best technology is the one that feels natural to the user.
                More than just writing code, I build modern web apps and cross-platform desktop applications that solve real business problems.
                My primary focus is removing technical complexity to emphasize the essence of functionality and
                aesthetics.
            </p>

            <h3 class="about-section-heading">Services &amp; Expertise</h3>
            <div class="about-services">
                <ul class="about-list">
                    <li>Modern Web App Development (React.js, Next.js, Astro.js)</li>
                    <li>Cross-Platform Desktop Applications (Electron.js)</li>
                </ul>
                <ul class="about-list">
                    <li>Responsive UI/UX Design</li>
                    <li>Backend Development (Node.js)</li>
                </ul>
            </div>

            <h3 class="about-section-heading">Key Technologies</h3>
            <div class="about-tags">
                {skills.map((skill) => (
                    <span>{skill}</span>
                ))}
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>
